; In a transaction that exchanges two commodities, without stating a cost
; or leaving a posting blank, Ledger normally prices the commodity of the
; first posting in the other.  When the first posting holds neither
; commodity, as balanced virtual budget lines in a third one do, it
; prices the commodity that entered the transaction's balance first.
; Ledger adds up the real postings in order, and at the first posting in
; a second commodity the sum of the postings before it enters the balance
; first, unless it is zero: a zero sum never enters, and the first to
; enter is then the commodity of the first non-zero posting from there on.
; Either way, when only one of the two is already a price target, that one
; is the price (#1130).
;
; The first transaction moves 50 EUR from the bank to the wallet before
; buying 100 GBP for 115 EUR.  The move sums to zero, so GBP enters first
; and is priced in EUR, at 1.15 EUR, and the lot goes on Assets:GBP.  The
; second is the first without its budget lines, in SEK and CHF: it prices
; SEK, the commodity of its first posting.  The third is the first in DKK
; and NOK, with a 10 DKK fee paid before buying NOK, so the sum is 10 DKK:
; DKK is priced in NOK, and the DKK postings become lots.  Each
; transaction exchanges its own pair of currencies, so that none is a
; price target yet.  GBP and SEK sort after the other currency and DKK
; before it, so no fixed order of the two components can pass for the rule
; in all three transactions, and neither can the order in which a balance
; keeps them, which changes from run to run.
;
; Ledger 3.4.1 summed the budget lines with the real postings, so the
; dollars were the zero sum, EUR entered first, and the first transaction
; priced EUR in GBP.

2024/01/05 Exchange after a transfer
    [Budget:Travel]          $100
    [Budget:Available]      $-100
    Assets:Wallet:EUR        50 EUR
    Assets:Bank:EUR         -50 EUR
    Assets:GBP              100 GBP
    Assets:Bank:EUR        -115 EUR

2024/01/06 Exchange after a transfer, without budget lines
    Assets:Wallet:SEK        50 SEK
    Assets:Bank:SEK         -50 SEK
    Assets:CHF              100 CHF
    Assets:Bank:SEK        -115 SEK

2024/01/07 Exchange after a transfer and a fee
